  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "If $cot\u2061x=\\sqrt{5}$ for some $x$, then find the value of $2\\sqrt{5}cot\u2061(x-3\\pi )-8.$",
  "worked_solution": "The period of $y=cot\u2061x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\ncot\u2061x=cot\u2061(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-3$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot\u2061x=cot\u2061(x+(-3)\\cdot \\pi )=cot\u2061(x-3\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $cot\u2061x=\\sqrt{5},$ then $cot\u2061(x-3\\pi )=\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{5}cot\u2061(x-3\\pi )-8 & =2\\sqrt{5}(\\sqrt{5})-8 \\\\  & =2{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}-8 \\\\  & =10-8 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
